Below is a summary of what’s going on, and then three *SEARCH/REPLACE* patches that add an “expressive” variant to both Button (so you get a 16 px/48 px button) and List (so you get a 16 px/24 px list).

---

## 1. Bug Scenario & Root Cause

• In the new “expressive” theme the **button** should render at **16 px font size** and **48 px height**, and **all** variants (primary, secondary, ghost, danger, etc.) should be available in expressive size.  
• In the new “expressive” theme the **list** should render at **16 px font size**, **24 px line height**.  
• **Right now** our component configs and React wrappers only know about “default”, “field” (md), “small” (sm), and the legacy “lg/xl/2xl” sizes.  
• **We need** to add an `"expressive"` size into the **.config.js** files so that the stories/documentation appear, and into the **React** components so that the proper CSS class (`--expressive`) gets applied.

